{"hits": {"hits": [{"created": "2026-10-07T04:45:51.624551+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-10T21:27:22.109563+00:00", "id": 23203143, "conceptrecid": "23203142", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23203143", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23203142", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23203143", "metadata": {"title": "Two consequences of group-algebra and planar Fourier certificates: wreath products and triangle bounds", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23203143", "publication_date": "2026-10-06", "description": "We derive two separately motivated consequences of precisely identified input theorems in OpenAI's mathematics collection. The torsion-free group-algebra counterexample, combined with the established Hopfian embedding framework, yields a finitely generated Hopfian group H for which the standard restricted regular wreath product C2 wr H is non-Hopfian. We give its split epimorphism and kernel explicitly. The sharp planar two-point Fourier certificate, combined with the Cohn-de Laat-Salmon product-program comparison and triangular-lattice Poisson bounds, yields L2=2/sqrt(3) and the exact planar triangle infimum P2=4/3. We reconstruct the deductions, audit the substantive inputs, repair product-proof bookkeeping, and provide independently implemented validated computations and source records. These consequences use credited literature; no first-priority or independent-breakthrough claim is made. The planar equality does not settle the all-dimensional triangle problem or assert attainment of its infimum. AI tools were used extensively in research, drafting, computation and verification. Internal independent and adversarial reviews were AI-assisted. This preprint has not undergone conventional human peer review or refereeing. AI systems are not authors; no external endorsement is implied. The associated Lean artifacts concern another construction and do not formally verify these results.", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Kriebel, Alec", "affiliation": "Independent researcher", "orcid": "0009-0001-9320-500X"}], "keywords": ["Hopfian groups", "restricted regular wreath products", "direct finiteness", "Cohn-Elkies bounds", "planar circle packing", "triangle three-point bounds", "group algebras", "non-Hopfian groups", "split epimorphisms", "Kourovka Notebook Problem 21.22", "sphere packing", "Fourier analysis", "Poisson summation", "linear programming bounds", "Schwartz functions", "triangular lattice", "positive definite kernels"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/A-Torsion-Free-Group-Algebra-That-Is-Not-Directly-Finite-October-4-2026/direct-finiteness.pdf", "relation": "references", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/A-sharp-Fourier-certificate-for-planar-circle-packing-September-23-2026/paper.pdf", "relation": "references", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "10.1007/s00209-024-03589-3", "relation": "references", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2206.15373v1", "relation": "references", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "10.4007/annals.2003.157.689", "relation": "references", "scheme": "doi"}], "version": "1.0.0", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23203142"}}]}}, "title": "Two consequences of group-algebra and planar Fourier certificates: wreath products and triangle bounds", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23203143", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23203143", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23203143?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23203143", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23203143", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23203143", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23203143/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23203142", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23203142", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23203142", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23203142", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23203143/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23203143/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23203143/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23203143/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23203143:preprint.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23203143:preprint.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23203143:preprint.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23203143:preprint.pdf/full/%5E250,/0/default.jpg", "750": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23203143:preprint.pdf/full/%5E750,/0/default.jpg", "1200": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23203143:preprint.pdf/full/%5E1200,/0/default.jpg"}, "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23203143/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23203143/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23203143/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23203143/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23203143/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23203143/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23203143/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23203143/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23203143/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23203143/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23203143/communities-suggestions", "request_deletion": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23203143/reque